cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "RegimeShift: known-boundary MDL detectors for cyclic categorical regime changes"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Mayo
    given-names: Mac
repository-code: "https://github.com/MacMayo1993/RegimeShift"
license: MIT
version: 3.1.0
abstract: >-
  Reference implementation and test harness for a known-boundary minimum
  description length comparison of categorical cyclic regime changes. It
  distinguishes unrestricted independent change, independent change within the
  fundamental invariant subspace, and shared-state exact-orbit transitions, and
  adds an approximate-orbit model interpolating between the last two. The
  shared-orbit alternative introduces no additional continuous parameter across
  the boundary and therefore carries no leading log n continuous-dimension
  penalty, paying only a discrete nonidentity-shift label cost. The advantage is
  conditional on structural correctness and is evaluated under common null
  calibration. This is a methodological simulation study; no real dataset is
  analysed.
keywords:
  - minimum description length
  - changepoint
  - cyclic groups
  - representation theory
  - information geometry
  - model selection
references:
  - type: article
    title: >-
      Geometric Complexity in Cyclic Regime Changes: Full,
      Fundamental-Subspace, and Shared-Orbit Models under Minimum Description
      Length
    authors:
      - family-names: Mayo
        given-names: Mac
    year: 2026
    notes: "The manuscript this repository implements; included in docs/."
